warning: em dash `—` in doc comment
  --> $DIR/fixture.rs:LL:CC
   |
LL | /// Reads the manifest — and returns its package name.
   |                        ^
   |
   = note: a dash between two clauses leaves their relationship for the reader to work out, and marks a sentence carrying more than one idea
   = help: a mechanical swap silences this warning and leaves the phrasing in place; which fix suits the sentence is a judgement this warning cannot make
   = help: one idea per sentence is what reads easily, so a dash is often a sign the sentence wants dividing rather than repunctuating
   = help: where the clause after the dash elaborates the one before it, a colon names that relationship
   = help: where both clauses stand on their own, a semicolon joins them or a full stop makes them two sentences
   = help: where a pair of dashes fences an aside, commas fold it in or a sentence of its own carries it
   = note: `#[warn(perfectionist::em_dash_prose)]` on by default

